{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>These are the reckonings.</b> In this section were counted all the weights of the donation of the Tabernacle — for silver, for gold, and for copper — and all its utensils for all its service were counted." "<b>The Tabernacle of the Tabernacle.</b> Twice — an allusion to the Temple that was taken as collateral through two destructions, for the sins of Israel (Tanchuma)." "<b>The Tabernacle of the Testimony.</b> A testimony to Israel that the Holy One, blessed be He, forgave them for the matter of the calf — for His Shekhinah dwelt among them." "<b>The service of the Levites.</b> The reckonings of the Tabernacle and its utensils — that is the service entrusted to the Levites in the wilderness: to carry, to take down, and to set up, each man according to the load assigned upon him, as stated in the section Naso." "<b>By the hand of Itamar.</b> He was the officer over them, to assign to each father's house the service upon it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:50.756135523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}